; Rhumb Workflow Protocol (RWP) - Sequence Format Grammar
; ABNF Specification for Phase Sequence Notation
; RFC 5234 Augmented Backus-Naur Form
;
; This grammar defines the formal syntax for phase sequence strings,
; which are used to describe the execution ordering and dependencies
; of RWP phases.

; === Top-level sequence expression ===
sequence           = logical-expr

; === Logical operators (precedence: AND > OR) ===
logical-expr       = or-expr

or-expr            = and-expr *( "," and-expr )

and-expr           = primary-expr *( "+" primary-expr )

; === Primary expressions ===
primary-expr       = phase-group
                   / phase-id
                   / "(" logical-expr ")"

; === Phase groups (for parallel/serial organization) ===
phase-group        = "[" logical-expr "]"

; === Phase identifiers ===
phase-id           = phase-number [ "-" sub-phase ]

phase-number       = "P-" 2DIGIT     ; e.g., P-01, P-02, ..., P-99

sub-phase          = %x41-5A          ; uppercase A-Z in validators/parsers

; === Comments (informational, not parsed) ===
comment            = ";" *( %x20-7E )  ; semicolon to end of line

; === Whitespace (ignored) ===
WSP                = %x20 / %x09      ; space or tab
CRLF               = %x0D %x0A        ; carriage return, line feed
LF                 = %x0A             ; line feed

DIGIT              = %x30-39          ; 0-9
ALPHA              = %x41-5A / %x61-7A ; A-Z / a-z

; === Examples of valid sequences ===
;
; P-01                          Single phase
; P-01, P-02                    Sequential phases (P-01 OR P-02)
; P-01 + P-02                   Parallel phases (P-01 AND P-02)
; P-01, (P-02 + P-03), P-04     P-01 first, then P-02 and P-03 in parallel, then P-04
; [P-01-A, P-01-B, P-01-C]      All sub-phases of P-01 (logical grouping)
; P-01 + [P-02-A, P-02-B]       P-01 in parallel with sub-phases P-02-A and P-02-B
;
; === Interpretation Rules ===
;
; 1. Comma (,) represents OR / sequential execution
;    Phases separated by commas execute one after another
;    P-01, P-02 means: complete P-01, then start P-02
;
; 2. Plus (+) represents AND / parallel execution
;    Phases separated by plus execute concurrently
;    P-01 + P-02 means: start P-01 and P-02 simultaneously
;
; 3. Parentheses group expressions
;    (P-01, P-02) + P-03 means: complete P-01 and P-02 in sequence, then start P-03 in parallel
;
; 4. Square brackets denote logical grouping
;    [P-01-A, P-01-B] groups sub-phases for readability
;
; === Precedence (high to low) ===
;
; 1. Parentheses & brackets: (expr) [expr]
; 2. AND (plus): expr1 + expr2
; 3. OR (comma): expr1, expr2
;
; Note: AND binds tighter than OR
; P-01, P-02 + P-03 = P-01, (P-02 + P-03)
;
; === Phase ID Constraints ===
;
; Valid examples:
; - P-01, P-02, P-03, ..., P-99 (two-digit phase numbers)
; - P-01-A, P-01-B, P-01-C, P-01-Z (sub-phases)
; - Mixed: P-01, P-02-A, P-03
;
; Invalid examples:
; - P-1 (must use two digits)
; - P-01-a (sub-phase letters must be uppercase)
; - p-01 (lowercase not allowed)
; - P-100 (only two-digit phase numbers)
;
; === Grammar Extensions ===
;
; Future versions may support:
; - Duration annotations: P-01{45} (45-minute phase)
; - Conditional branches: P-01 ? P-02-A : P-02-B (if/else)
; - Quantifiers: P-01* (zero or more), P-01+ (one or more)
;
; These are reserved for future use and not yet supported in RWP.
